#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
"""firecrawl-router — Firecrawl REST API with a self-hosted primary and a commercial fallback.

Usage:
  firecrawl-router [--listen HOST:PORT] -- firecrawl-mcp [ARGS...]
  firecrawl-router [--listen HOST:PORT]            # serve only, for tests: no token check, loopback --listen only

With a child command, the router listens on a loopback port (ephemeral by
default), starts the child with FIRECRAWL_API_URL pointing at itself and
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY set to a random per-process token, and exits with the
child. The child never sees either real key.

Each request goes to the primary (self-hosted). It is retried once on the
fallback (commercial) when the primary:
  1. cannot be reached or times out;
  2. answers 404 (route not in self-hosted Firecrawl: agent, monitor, ...) or 5xx;
  3. scrapes a bot wall: a page whose own status is 202 or 405 (AWS WAF's challenge and
     CAPTCHA), 403, 429 or 503, or a short page whose text is a challenge (Cloudflare,
     Akamai, DataDome, HUMAN/PerimeterX, Imperva, Vercel, AWS WAF, F5);
  4. maps 0 links, or searches 0 results.
A fallback that also fails returns the primary's answer (or the fallback's,
when the primary was unreachable). Never the other way round: the fallback's
429 or 402 never sends work to the primary.

LLM formats (2026-10-18). Self-hosted Firecrawl has no LLM, so a scrape that asks for the
`query` or `json` format would fail there, and the commercial API is not used. The router
strips those formats from the upstream request, takes the markdown from the primary and
runs the model itself, in this order (first rung that answers wins):
  1. SIPB LLMs (via the local sipb-llms-proxy), when the page fits ~24k tokens;
  2. the same model, chunked: each chunk is mapped, the partial results are reduced. A page
     past that is never sent whole, because the SIPB server silently keeps only the LAST 16k
     tokens of a prompt over ~32k (no error). A reply whose `usage.prompt_tokens` is far below
     the size sent counts as truncated and falls through;
  3. the free large-context LiteLLM pool (gemini-free, then gemini-free-lite).
When every rung fails, the page's markdown is returned with a `warning` instead of an error.
The answer goes in `data.answer` (query) and `data.json` (json); the header X-Firecrawl-LLM
names the rung. FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_LLM=off passes the formats through untouched.

Developer search (2026-10-24). Self-hosted Firecrawl has no /v2/search/developer (a 404) and ignores
categories ["developer"] on /v2/search (an empty `web` list). With no commercial fallback configured the router
answers both itself from the GitHub search API: issues, merged pull requests, READMEs, docs and code files,
merged round-robin into Firecrawl's response shape plus `source: "github"`, a per-kind `coverage` and a
`warning` when a kind could not be searched. GitHub's rate-limit headers close the code-search (10/min) or
general search (30/min) bucket until its reset; all buckets closed is a 429 with Retry-After, any other total
failure a 502. `types` (issue, pull_request, readme, doc), `repos`, `language`, `k` and `passages` are honoured;
`sources`, `skills`, `license`, `topic`, `min_stars`, `max_stars`, `archived` and `fork` are a 400. With a
commercial fallback configured the request goes to the primary and the fallback as before.
PUBLIC REPOSITORIES ONLY: the GITHUB_TOKEN behind it is a classic PAT that can read private repositories and this
listener has no caller authentication, so issue and PR queries carry `is:public` and a code hit is dropped unless
GitHub reports its repository as not private. A fine-grained read-only public-repository token under its own
secretspec name (FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_GITHUB_SECRET) removes the dependence on those two filters. At most two searches
run at once, all inside FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_SEARCH_TIMEOUT.

Async jobs (crawl, batch scrape, extract) stay on the backend that created
them: the router remembers job id -> backend and rewrites absolute `url`/`next`
links in responses to point back at itself.

Environment:
  FIRECRAWL_SELFHOST_URL       primary base URL (required)
  FIRECRAWL_SELFHOST_API_KEY   primary bearer token (optional)
  FIRECRAWL_FALLBACK_URL       fallback base URL (default https://api.firecrawl.dev)
  FIRECRAWL_API_KEY            fallback key; empty disables the fallback
  FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_FALLBACK    "off" disables the fallback
  FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_TIMEOUT     floor for the per-request timeout, seconds (default 120)
  FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_SEARCH_TIMEOUT
                               hard cap for /search (and /v2/search), seconds (default 35).
                               SearXNG engine stalls on Hyades's shared egress used to hold
                               the router for the full 120 s floor, which blew past Cursor's
                               MCP idle limit (-32001) with commercial fallback off (2026-10-22).
  FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_LLM         "off" disables LLM-format handling (default on)
  FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_SIPB_KEY    SIPB LLMs key (MIT_SIPB_API_KEY); BASE default http://127.0.0.1:8890/api,
                               MODEL default qwen3.6:35b-a3b-q4_K_M (…_SIPB_BASE, …_SIPB_MODEL)
  FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_LITELLM_KEY LiteLLM key; BASE default http://127.0.0.1:4000/v1, models gemini-free,
                               gemini-free-lite (…_LITELLM_BASE, …_LITELLM_MODELS, comma list)
  FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_LLM_DEADLINE seconds to spend on one scrape's extraction (default 240: under
                               Claude Code's 300 s MCP idle limit with room for the scrape itself)
  FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_DEVELOPER   "off" disables the GitHub-backed developer search (default on)
  FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_GITHUB_KEY  GitHub token; empty (the default) reads the secretspec name below with
                               `sudo-secretspec get` once and holds it in memory (read again at most once a minute
                               while it holds none: a failed read, or a 401 dropped it);
                               no token at all: unauthenticated (10 req/min, no code search).
  FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_GITHUB_SECRET  that secretspec name (default GITHUB_TOKEN)
                               BASE default https://api.github.com (…_GITHUB_BASE)

The five base URLs above (SELFHOST, FALLBACK, SIPB, LITELLM, GITHUB) must each be https:// or loopback http
(127.0.0.1, localhost, ::1) with a plain host[:port] (no userinfo), checked at startup; no variable lifts that.

A bearer key is set as an unredirected header and no request follows a redirect: a 3xx from a backend is
a failure (fallback reason "redirect refused"), and a client's request target must start with "/" and leave
the base URL's host unchanged (else HTTP 400), so a key never reaches a host the base URL did not name
(https to whatever host a repointed base names is still allowed).

--open drops the bearer token, so local programs that speak the Firecrawl API
(Hermes' firecrawl web backend) can use the router at a fixed --listen address.
Every run without a token (--open, or serve only with no child command) refuses a
non-loopback --listen address: the router holds the backend keys.

One log line per request on stderr: method, path, backend, status, seconds and
the fallback reason. Keys are never logged.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import hmac
import ipaddress
import http.server
import json
import os
import re
import secrets
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import threading
import time
import urllib.error
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request
from dataclasses import dataclass

UUID_RE = re.compile(r"[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}")
ABS_API_LINK_RE = re.compile(r"^https?://[^/]+(/v\d+/.*)$")
BOT_WALL_STATUSES = {202, 403, 405, 429, 503}
# Keep in step with BLOCK_PATTERNS in bin/web-get. Matched only on a short page (a challenge
# interstitial), so an article that mentions "captcha" is not a bot wall.
BOT_WALL_RE = re.compile("|".join([
    r"just a moment\.\.\.", r"attention required!? \| cloudflare", r"checking your browser",
    r"performing security verification", r"enable javascript and cookies to continue",
    r"verify you are (a )?human", r"you have been blocked", r"received a high number of requests",
    r"powered and protected by", r"please enable js and disable any ad blocker",
    r"captcha-delivery\.com", r"press (&|and) hold", r"incapsula incident id",
    r"request unsuccessful\. incapsula", r"vercel security checkpoint",
    r"let'?s confirm you are human", r"awswaf", r"the requested url was rejected",
]), re.I)
BOT_WALL_MAX_CHARS = 5000
HOP_HEADERS = {
    "connection", "keep-alive", "proxy-authenticate", "proxy-authorization", "te",
    "trailers", "transfer-encoding", "upgrade", "host", "content-length",
    "authorization", "accept-encoding",
}
MAX_JOBS = 10000


@dataclass
class Backend:
    name: str
    base: str
    key: str


@dataclass
class Reply:
    status: int
    headers: dict
    body: bytes
    error: str = ""

    def json(self):
        try:
            return json.loads(self.body)
        except (ValueError, UnicodeDecodeError):
            return None


class _NoRedirect(urllib.request.HTTPRedirectHandler):
    """A request with a bearer key must never follow a redirect to another host or path."""

    def redirect_request(self, req, fp, code, msg, headers, newurl):
        return None


def _open(req, timeout):
    return urllib.request.build_opener(_NoRedirect).open(req, timeout=timeout)


LOOPBACK_URL_HOSTS = ("127.0.0.1", "localhost", "::1")  # hostnames in a base URL; --listen spellings are separate


def _origin(url: str) -> str:
    """scheme://host[:port] of a rejected or logged URL: never its userinfo, path or query, which may carry a key."""
    try:
        u = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url.strip())
        host = f"[{u.hostname}]" if u.hostname and ":" in u.hostname else u.hostname
        if not (u.scheme and host):
            return "(not a URL)"
        return f"{u.scheme}://{host}" + (f":{u.port}" if u.port else "")
    except ValueError:
        return "(not a URL)"


def _check_base(name: str, url: str) -> str:
    """A base URL that receives a key: https, or http to loopback; no userinfo, backslash or whitespace.

    urllib dials Request.host, which keeps userinfo and backslashes that urlparse().hostname drops
    (`http://evil.example@127.0.0.1` parses as 127.0.0.1), so the netloc is held to a plain host[:port].
    """
    try:
        u = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url)
        _ = u.port  # raises ValueError on a bad port
    except ValueError:
        u = None
    ok = (u is not None and u.hostname
          and not any(c.isspace() for c in url)
          and "@" not in u.netloc and "\\" not in u.netloc
          and u.username is None and u.password is None
          and (u.scheme == "https" or (u.scheme == "http" and u.hostname in LOOPBACK_URL_HOSTS)))
    if not ok:
        sys.exit(f"firecrawl-router: {name} must be https:// or a loopback http:// URL "
                 f"(host[:port] only: no userinfo, backslash or whitespace), not {_origin(url)}")
    return url


def call(backend: Backend, method: str, path: str, headers: dict, body: bytes | None,
         timeout: float) -> Reply:
    # `path` is a client's raw request target: ".evil.example/x" or ":1/x" appended to a base URL changes the
    # host the key goes to, so it must start with "/" and leave the base's netloc as it was.
    url = backend.base + path
    try:
        same_host = path.startswith("/") and (urllib.parse.urlsplit(url).netloc
                                              == urllib.parse.urlsplit(backend.base).netloc)
    except ValueError:
        same_host = False
    if not same_host:
        return Reply(0, {}, b"", "refused: the request target must be a path on the configured backend")
    hdrs = {k: v for k, v in headers.items() if k.lower() not in HOP_HEADERS}
    req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=body, headers=hdrs, method=method)
    if backend.key:
        req.add_unredirected_header("Authorization", f"Bearer {backend.key}")
    try:
        with _open(req, timeout) as r:
            return Reply(r.status, dict(r.headers), r.read())
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        if 300 <= e.code < 400:
            return Reply(0, {}, b"", f"redirect refused (HTTP {e.code})")
        return Reply(e.code, dict(e.headers or {}), e.read() or b"")
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 - any transport failure is a fallback reason
        return Reply(0, {}, b"", f"{type(e).__name__}: {e}")


def fallback_reason(path: str, reply: Reply) -> str:
    if reply.status == 0:
        return f"unreachable ({reply.error})"
    if reply.status == 404:
        return "404 (route not on this backend)"
    if reply.status >= 500:
        return f"HTTP {reply.status}"
    if reply.status != 200:
        return ""
    doc = reply.json()
    if not isinstance(doc, dict):
        return ""
    data = doc.get("data")
    route = path.split("?", 1)[0].rstrip("/")
    if route.endswith("/scrape") and isinstance(data, dict):
        code = (data.get("metadata") or {}).get("statusCode")
        if code in BOT_WALL_STATUSES:
            return f"page status {code}"
        md = data.get("markdown")
        if isinstance(md, str) and len(md) < BOT_WALL_MAX_CHARS:
            m = BOT_WALL_RE.search(md)
            if m:
                return f"challenge page ({m.group(0)!r})"
    if route.endswith("/map"):
        links = doc.get("links") if "links" in doc else (data or {}).get("links") if isinstance(data, dict) else None
        if isinstance(links, list) and not links:
            return "map returned 0 links"
    if route.endswith("/search"):
        if isinstance(data, list) and not data:
            return "search returned 0 results"
        if isinstance(data, dict) and not any(isinstance(v, list) and v for v in data.values()):
            return "search returned 0 results"
    return ""


def request_timeout(body: bytes | None, floor: float, *, cap: float | None = None) -> float:
    try:
        ms = json.loads(body or b"{}").get("timeout")
    except (ValueError, AttributeError):
        ms = None
    if isinstance(ms, (int, float)) and ms > 0:
        t = max(floor, ms / 1000 + 30)
    else:
        t = floor
    if cap is not None:
        t = min(t, cap)
    return t


def search_path(path: str) -> bool:
    return path.split("?", 1)[0].rstrip("/").endswith("/search")


def dev_route(method: str, path: str, body: bytes | None) -> str:
    """"direct" for GET|POST /v2/search/developer; "category" for POST /v2/search with categories ["developer"]."""
    route = path.split("?", 1)[0].rstrip("/")
    if method in ("GET", "POST") and route == "/v2/search/developer":
        return "direct"
    if method == "POST" and route == "/v2/search":
        try:
            doc = json.loads(body or b"{}")
        except ValueError:
            return ""
        if isinstance(doc, dict) and doc.get("categories") == ["developer"]:
            return "category"
    return ""


# ---- developer search (GitHub-backed, 2026-10-24) -------------------------------------------
# Self-hosted Firecrawl has no /v2/search/developer and ignores categories ["developer"] on
# /v2/search (a 404 and an empty `web` list). With no commercial fallback the router answers both
# itself from the GitHub search API, in Firecrawl's response shape plus a `source` field.
DEV_TYPES = ("issue", "pull_request", "readme", "doc")  # Firecrawl's four result kinds
DEV_CODE = "code"                                       # ours: a source file that is no README or doc
DEV_UNSUPPORTED = ("sources", "skills", "license", "topic", "min_stars", "max_stars", "archived", "fork")
DEV_ORDER = ("readme", "doc", "pull_request", "issue", DEV_CODE)  # round-robin order of the merged ranking
DEV_DOC_EXTS = {"md", "mdx", "markdown", "rst", "adoc", "txt"}
DEV_STOPWORDS = frozenset("a an and are as at be but by can could do does for from how i if in into is it its my "
                          "of on or so that the this to was we what when where which who why with would you your".split())
DEV_REPO_RE = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+")
DEV_LANG_RE = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9_+#.-]{1,30}")
DEV_TERM_RE = re.compile(r"[\w.+#/-]+")  # no ":", quote or space: a query can never smuggle in a GitHub qualifier
DEV_MAX_TERMS = 8
DEV_MAX_TERM_CHARS = 64
DEV_MAX_Q = 256        # GitHub refuses a longer q with 422
DEV_MAX_REPO_CHARS = 120
DEV_PASSAGE_CHARS = 700
DEV_SLOTS = 2          # searches in flight at once: each is up to three GitHub calls on one token
SECRETSPEC = "/usr/local/bin/sudo-secretspec"


def dev_terms(query: str) -> list[str]:
    out: list[str] = []
    for t in DEV_TERM_RE.findall(query):
        t = t.strip(".-/")[:DEV_MAX_TERM_CHARS]
        if len(t) < 2 or t.lower() in DEV_STOPWORDS or t in ("AND", "OR", "NOT") or t in out:
            continue
        out.append(t)
    return out[:DEV_MAX_TERMS]


def dev_loosen(terms: list[str]) -> list[str]:
    """Half of the terms, the longest ones, in their original order: GitHub ANDs every term."""
    if len(terms) <= 2:
        return []
    keep = sorted(range(len(terms)), key=lambda i: -len(terms[i]))[: max(2, len(terms) // 2)]
    return [terms[i] for i in sorted(keep)]


def _dev_list(v) -> list[str]:
    """A repeatable filter: a JSON list, or `a,b` / repeated query values."""
    vals = v if isinstance(v, list) else [] if v is None else [v]
    return [p.strip() for x in vals for p in str(x).split(",") if p.strip()]


def _dev_int(v, default: int) -> int | None:
    """An absent value is the default; an int (never a bool or float) or a short digit string is itself; else None."""
    if v is None:
        return default
    if type(v) is int:
        return v
    return int(v) if isinstance(v, str) and v.isdigit() and len(v) <= 6 else None


def parse_dev_request(method: str, path: str, body: bytes | None) -> tuple[dict | None, str]:
    """(params, "") or (None, why the request is refused with HTTP 400)."""
    if method == "GET":
        raw = {k: v if len(v) > 1 else v[0] for k, v in urllib.parse.parse_qs(urllib.parse.urlsplit(path).query).items()}
    else:
        try:
            raw = json.loads(body or b"{}")
        except ValueError:
            raw = None
        if not isinstance(raw, dict):
            return None, "the body must be a JSON object"
    for name in DEV_UNSUPPORTED:
        v = raw.get(name)
        if v is not None and v != "" and v != [] and v is not False:
            return None, f"{name} is not supported by the GitHub-backed developer search"
    query = raw.get("query")
    if not isinstance(query, str) or not dev_terms(query):
        return None, "query must be a string with at least one searchable word"
    k, passages = _dev_int(raw.get("k"), 10), _dev_int(raw.get("passages"), 1)
    if k is None or passages is None:
        return None, "k and passages must be integers"
    if not 1 <= k <= 100 or not 1 <= passages <= 5:
        return None, "k must be 1-100 and passages 1-5"
    types = _dev_list(raw.get("types")) or None
    if types and not set(types) <= set(DEV_TYPES):
        return None, f"types must be among {', '.join(DEV_TYPES)}"
    repos = _dev_list(raw.get("repos"))
    if not all(DEV_REPO_RE.fullmatch(r) for r in repos):
        return None, "repos must be owner/name slugs"
    if len(" ".join(f"repo:{r}" for r in repos)) > DEV_MAX_REPO_CHARS:
        return None, f"repos is too long: the repo: qualifiers may take {DEV_MAX_REPO_CHARS} characters of GitHub's {DEV_MAX_Q}"
    language = raw.get("language")
    if language is not None and not (isinstance(language, str) and DEV_LANG_RE.fullmatch(language)):
        return None, "language must be a plain language name"
    return {"query": query, "k": k, "passages": passages, "types": types, "repos": repos,
            "language": language}, ""


def read_secret(name: str, secretspec: str = SECRETSPEC) -> str:
    """One value from sudo-secretspec, held in memory by the caller; never logged, never in argv."""
    try:
        out = subprocess.run([secretspec, "get", name, "--reason", "firecrawl-router developer search"],
                             stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True, timeout=20)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return ""
    return out.stdout.decode("utf-8", "replace").strip() if out.returncode == 0 else ""


@dataclass
class GHReply:
    status: int                 # 0 = no HTTP answer
    doc: dict | None = None
    limited_for: float = 0.0    # seconds until the bucket this call hit refills
    error: str = ""


class DevSearch:
    """Ranked developer results (issues, merged PRs, READMEs, docs, code) from the GitHub search API.

    Public repositories only: issue and PR queries carry `is:public`, and a code hit counts only when GitHub says
    its repository is not private (the token behind it can read private repositories, and the router listener
    has no caller authentication). Three calls per search at most (issues, merged PRs, code), each retried once
    with fewer terms when it finds nothing, all inside one deadline. GitHub keeps separate per-minute buckets for
    code search (10) and the rest (30), so each response's X-RateLimit-* and Retry-After headers close a bucket
    until its reset instead of being retried.
    """

    def __init__(self, base: str, token: str = "", secret: str = "GITHUB_TOKEN", timeout: float = 15.0,
                 secretspec: str = SECRETSPEC, budget: float = 35.0):
        self.base, self.timeout, self.budget = base.rstrip("/"), timeout, budget
        self._token, self._static = token, bool(token)
        self._secret, self._secretspec = secret, secretspec
        self._last_read = 0.0
        self._closed: dict[str, float] = {}  # bucket -> monotonic time it reopens
        self._lock = threading.Lock()
        self._read_lock = threading.Lock()   # one secretspec read at a time; later callers see its result
        self._slots = threading.BoundedSemaphore(DEV_SLOTS)

    def token(self) -> str:
        with self._lock:
            if self._token or self._static:
                return self._token
        with self._read_lock:
            with self._lock:
                if self._token:
                    return self._token
                if self._last_read and time.monotonic() - self._last_read < 60:
                    return ""
            value = read_secret(self._secret, self._secretspec)
            with self._lock:
                self._last_read = time.monotonic()
                self._token = value
                return value

    def _gh(self, endpoint: str, q: str, per_page: int, deadline: float, token: str) -> GHReply:
        bucket = "code_search" if endpoint == "code" else "search"
        with self._lock:
            wait = self._closed.get(bucket, 0.0) - time.monotonic()
        if wait > 0:
            return GHReply(0, limited_for=wait, error=f"{bucket} rate limit, {wait:.0f}s left")
        timeout = min(self.timeout, deadline - time.monotonic())
        if timeout < 0.5:
            return GHReply(0, error="deadline")
        req = urllib.request.Request(
            f"{self.base}/search/{endpoint}?" + urllib.parse.urlencode({"q": q, "per_page": per_page}),
            headers={"Accept": "application/vnd.github.text-match+json", "User-Agent": "firecrawl-router",
                     "X-GitHub-Api-Version": "2022-11-28"})
        if token:
            req.add_unredirected_header("Authorization", f"Bearer {token}")
        try:
            with _open(req, timeout) as r:
                status, hdrs, raw = r.status, {k.lower(): v for k, v in r.headers.items()}, r.read()
        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
            status, hdrs, raw = e.code, {k.lower(): v for k, v in (e.headers or {}).items()}, e.read() or b""
        except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 - any transport failure is one failed rung
            return GHReply(0, error=f"{type(e).__name__}")
        wait = 0.0
        retry_after, remaining, reset = hdrs.get("retry-after"), hdrs.get("x-ratelimit-remaining"), hdrs.get("x-ratelimit-reset")
        limited = status == 429 or (status == 403 and (retry_after or remaining == "0" or b"rate limit" in raw.lower()))
        if limited or remaining == "0":
            try:
                wait = float(retry_after) if retry_after else max(1.0, float(reset) - time.time())
            except (TypeError, ValueError):
                wait = 60.0
            with self._lock:
                self._closed[bucket] = time.monotonic() + wait
        if status == 401 and token:
            with self._lock:  # revoked or rotated: drop it so the next search re-reads (at most once a minute)
                if not self._static and self._token == token:
                    self._token = ""
        if status != 200:
            return GHReply(status, limited_for=wait if limited else 0.0, error=f"HTTP {status}")
        try:
            doc = json.loads(raw)
        except ValueError:
            return GHReply(status, error="not JSON")
        return GHReply(status, doc if isinstance(doc, dict) else None)

    def _query(self, endpoint: str, terms: list[str], scope: str, p: dict, per_page: int, deadline: float,
               token: str) -> GHReply:
        extra = " ".join([scope] + [f"repo:{r}" for r in p["repos"]] + ([f"language:{p['language']}"] if p["language"] else []))
        reply = None
        for i, attempt in enumerate((terms, dev_loosen(terms))):
            # a scoped search never retries: whether a guessed repo (private ones included) holds all the terms must not
            # show in how many calls or how long the answer took
            if not attempt or (i and (p["repos"] or deadline - time.monotonic() < 3)):
                break
            room = DEV_MAX_Q - len(extra) - 1
            while len(" ".join(attempt)) > room and len(attempt) > 1:
                attempt = attempt[:-1]
            r = self._gh(endpoint, f"{' '.join(attempt)[:room]} {extra}".strip(), per_page, deadline, token)
            if r.status == 422 and p["repos"]:  # GitHub says 422 for a repo that does not exist (or the token cannot see)
                r = GHReply(200, {"items": []})
            if reply is None or r.status == 200:  # a failed retry never replaces an empty 200
                reply = r
            if r.status != 200 or (r.doc or {}).get("items"):
                break
        return reply or GHReply(0, error="no terms")

    def search(self, p: dict) -> tuple[int, dict, str]:
        """(HTTP status, Firecrawl-shaped document, one-line note for the log)."""
        busy = (429, {"success": False, "source": "github", "retryAfter": 5,
                      "error": "GitHub developer search is busy; retry in 5s"}, "busy")
        deadline = time.monotonic() + self.budget
        if not self._slots.acquire(timeout=min(5.0, self.budget)):
            return busy
        try:
            if deadline - time.monotonic() < self.budget * 0.25:  # a slot that came too late to finish a search
                return busy
            return self._search(p, deadline)
        finally:
            self._slots.release()

    def _search(self, p: dict, deadline: float) -> tuple[int, dict, str]:
        token = self.token()  # resolved here, once: the parallel calls below share it (and one secretspec read)
        authed = bool(token)
        wanted = set(p["types"] or (*DEV_TYPES, DEV_CODE))
        terms = dev_terms(p["query"])
        per_page = min(100, max(5, p["k"]))
        jobs: dict[str, tuple[str, str]] = {}
        if "issue" in wanted:
            jobs["issue"] = ("issues", "is:issue is:public")
        if "pull_request" in wanted:
            jobs["pull_request"] = ("issues", "is:pr is:merged is:public")
        if wanted & {"readme", "doc", DEV_CODE}:
            jobs[DEV_CODE] = ("code", "filename:README.md" if wanted & {"readme", "doc", DEV_CODE} == {"readme"} else "")
        shared: dict[str, GHReply] = {}

        def run(name: str) -> None:
            endpoint, scope = jobs[name]
            try:
                shared[name] = self._query(endpoint, terms, scope, p, per_page, deadline, token)
            except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 - one failed rung, never a crashed request
                shared[name] = GHReply(0, error=type(e).__name__)

        threads = [threading.Thread(target=run, args=(n,), daemon=True) for n in jobs]
        for t in threads:
            t.start()
        for t in threads:
            t.join(timeout=max(0.1, deadline - time.monotonic() + 1))
        replies = {name: shared.get(name) or GHReply(0, error="deadline") for name in jobs}  # a snapshot: a late thread cannot change it

        kept = dict.fromkeys(jobs, 0)

        buckets: dict[str, list[dict]] = {t: [] for t in DEV_ORDER}
        for name, reply in replies.items():
            for item in (reply.doc or {}).get("items") or []:
                try:
                    r = self._shape(name, item, p["passages"]) if isinstance(item, dict) else None
                except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 - an upstream item of an unexpected shape is skipped
                    r = None
                if r and r["type"] in wanted:
                    buckets[r["type"]].append(r)
                    kept[name] += 1
        results: list[dict] = []
        seen: set[str] = set()
        while len(results) < p["k"] and any(buckets.values()):
            for t in DEV_ORDER:
                if buckets[t] and len(results) < p["k"]:
                    r = buckets[t].pop(0)
                    if r["url"] not in seen:
                        seen.add(r["url"])
                        results.append(r)

        def state(kinds) -> str:
            names = [n for n in jobs if n in kinds]
            if not names:
                return "skipped"
            return "ok" if all(replies[n].status == 200 for n in names) else "unavailable"

        coverage = {"issue": state({"issue"}), "pull_request": state({"pull_request"}),
                    "readme": state({DEV_CODE}) if "readme" in wanted else "skipped",
                    "doc": state({DEV_CODE}) if "doc" in wanted else "skipped"}
        if DEV_CODE in wanted:
            coverage[DEV_CODE] = state({DEV_CODE})
        note = " ".join(f"{n}={kept[n] if replies[n].status == 200 else replies[n].error}" for n in jobs)
        failed = [n for n in jobs if replies[n].status != 200]
        if len(failed) == len(jobs):
            wait = max((replies[n].limited_for for n in failed), default=0.0)
            if wait > 0:
                return 429, {"success": False, "source": "github", "retryAfter": round(wait),
                             "error": f"GitHub search is rate limited; retry in {wait:.0f}s"}, note
            return 502, {"success": False, "source": "github",
                         "error": "GitHub search failed: " + ", ".join(sorted({replies[n].error for n in failed}))}, note
        doc = {"success": True, "source": "github", "results": results, "coverage": coverage, "reranked": False}
        warnings = [f"{n}: {replies[n].error}" for n in failed]
        if not authed:
            warnings.append("no GitHub token (GITHUB_TOKEN via sudo-secretspec): unauthenticated limits apply")
        if warnings:
            doc["warning"] = "; ".join(warnings)
        return 200, doc, note

    @staticmethod
    def _shape(job: str, item: dict, n_passages: int) -> dict | None:
        url = item.get("html_url")
        if not isinstance(url, str):
            return None
        if job == DEV_CODE and (item.get("repository") or {}).get("private") is not False:
            return None  # the token reads private repositories; only a repository GitHub calls public is returned
        want_prop = None if job == DEV_CODE else "body"  # an issue's title fragment only repeats its title
        frags = [m.get("fragment") for m in item.get("text_matches") or [] if isinstance(m, dict)
                 and isinstance(m.get("fragment"), str) and m["fragment"].strip()
                 and (want_prop is None or m.get("property") == want_prop)]
        if job == DEV_CODE:
            repo = (item.get("repository") or {}).get("full_name") or "?"
            path = item.get("path") or item.get("name") or "?"
            name = path.rsplit("/", 1)[-1].lower()
            stem, dot, ext = name.rpartition(".")
            if not dot:
                stem, ext = name, ""
            if stem == "readme" or stem.startswith("readme."):
                typ, rid = "readme", f"readme:{repo}" + (f":{path}" if "/" in path else "")
            elif ext in DEV_DOC_EXTS or path.lower().startswith(("docs/", "doc/")):
                typ, rid = "doc", f"doc:{repo}:{path}"
            else:
                typ, rid = DEV_CODE, f"code:{repo}:{path}"
                frags = [f"```{ext}\n{f.strip()}\n```" for f in frags]
            texts = [f[:DEV_PASSAGE_CHARS] for f in frags[:n_passages]]
            return {"id": rid, "type": typ, "url": url, "title": f"{repo}: {path}", "source": "github",
                    "passages": [{"text": t} for t in texts]}
        repo = str(item.get("repository_url") or "").rsplit("/repos/", 1)[-1]
        num = item.get("number")
        state = "merged" if job == "pull_request" else str(item.get("state") or "")
        head = f"{repo}#{num} · {state} · updated {str(item.get('updated_at') or '')[:10]}"
        if not frags:
            body = (item.get("body") or "").strip()
            frags = [body] if body else []
        texts = [f[:DEV_PASSAGE_CHARS] for f in frags[:n_passages]] or [""]
        texts[0] = f"{head}\n\n{texts[0]}".strip()
        return {"id": f"{job}:{repo}#{num}", "type": job, "url": url, "title": str(item.get("title") or url),
                "source": "github", "passages": [{"text": t} for t in texts]}


def dev_web_results(doc: dict) -> list[dict]:
    """The /v2/search `web` shape (category developer) for a developer-search document."""
    out = []
    for i, r in enumerate(doc.get("results") or [], 1):
        text = " ".join(((r.get("passages") or [{}])[0].get("text") or "").split())
        out.append({"url": r["url"], "title": r["title"], "description": text[:300], "position": i,
                    "category": "developer", "source": "github"})
    return out


# ---- LLM formats (query, json) -------------------------------------------------------------
CHARS_PER_TOKEN = 3.3  # conservative (real prose is ~4+): overestimates tokens, so budgets hold
SIPB_ONE_SHOT_CHARS = int(24000 * CHARS_PER_TOKEN)   # whole page in one call
SIPB_CHUNK_CHARS = int(16000 * CHARS_PER_TOKEN)      # one chunk of a map-reduce
BIG_ONE_SHOT_CHARS = 600_000                         # ~180k tokens; gemini's window is 1M
BIG_CHUNK_CHARS = 400_000
TRUNCATION_CHARS_PER_TOKEN = 5.0  # more chars per reported prompt token than this = cut short
TRUNCATION_MIN_CHARS = 40_000     # a smaller prompt is never cut (repetitive text tokenizes at 5+ chars/token)
TRUNCATION_CAP_TOKENS = 16386     # ollama halves a 32768 window and reports 16386 (ollama/ollama#17427)
LLM_MAX_TOKENS = 4096
LLM_NONE = "NONE"
LLM_SYS = "You answer questions about a web page. Use only the page content provided. Be concise."
LLM_QUOTE_SYS = ("Reply with ONE verbatim quote from the page that answers the question. "
                 "Output only the quote, nothing else. If nothing on the page answers it, reply exactly NONE.")
LLM_ABSTAIN = "The page does not contain an answer to this question."


class LLMError(Exception):
    pass


@dataclass
class Rung:
    name: str
    base: str
    key: str
    model: str
    one_shot: int
    chunk: int
    check_truncation: bool = False


def wanted_formats(doc: dict):
    """Split a scrape body's formats into (kept formats, [LLM wants]) -- None when it has none.

    A want is {"kind": "json"|"query", "prompt", "schema", "mode"}. Both encodings are read:
    the v2 object ({"type": "json", "prompt": ..., "schema": ...}) and the v1 string with a
    top-level jsonOptions/queryOptions."""
    formats = doc.get("formats")
    if not isinstance(formats, list):
        return None
    kept, wants = [], []
    for f in formats:
        kind = f.get("type") if isinstance(f, dict) else f
        if kind in ("json", "query"):
            opts = f if isinstance(f, dict) else (doc.get("jsonOptions" if kind == "json" else "queryOptions") or {})
            wants.append({"kind": kind, "prompt": str(opts.get("prompt") or ""),
                          "schema": opts.get("schema"), "mode": opts.get("mode") or "freeform"})
        else:
            kept.append(f)
    return (kept, wants) if wants else None


def split_chunks(text: str, size: int) -> list[str]:
    """Pieces of at most `size` chars, cut at a paragraph or line break when one is near."""
    out, i = [], 0
    while i < len(text):
        j = min(i + size, len(text))
        if j < len(text):
            for sep in ("\n\n", "\n", " "):
                k = text.rfind(sep, i + size // 2, j)
                if k > 0:
                    j = k + len(sep)
                    break
        out.append(text[i:j])
        i = j
    return out


def norm_text(s: str) -> str:
    return re.sub(r"\s+", " ", s.replace("`", "").replace("**", "")).strip().lower()


def parse_json_text(text: str):
    try:
        return json.loads(text)
    except ValueError:
        pass
    m = re.search(r"[\[{].*[\]}]", text, re.S)
    if m:
        try:
            return json.loads(m.group(0))
        except ValueError:
            pass
    raise LLMError("model did not return JSON")


class Extractor:
    """Runs the query/json formats over a page's markdown, rung by rung."""

    def __init__(self, rungs: list[Rung], deadline: float = 240.0, call_timeout: float = 240.0):
        self.rungs = rungs
        self.deadline = deadline
        self.call_timeout = call_timeout
        self.log = sys.stderr
        self._tl = threading.local()  # t_end of the scrape being served on this thread

    def chat(self, rung: Rung, system: str, user: str, schema=None, expect_json=False) -> str:
        if time.monotonic() > getattr(self._tl, "t_end", float("inf")):
            raise LLMError("deadline")
        body = {"model": rung.model, "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": LLM_MAX_TOKENS,
                "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": system}, {"role": "user", "content": user}]}
        if expect_json:
            body["response_format"] = ({"type": "json_schema", "json_schema": {"name": "extract", "strict": True, "schema": schema}}
                                       if isinstance(schema, dict) else {"type": "json_object"})
        for attempt in (1, 2):  # SIPB now and then returns an empty reply (2026-10-18): ask once more
            d = self._post(rung, body)
            if d is None and expect_json:  # server refused response_format: ask in the prompt alone
                body.pop("response_format")
                d = self._post(rung, body)
            if d is None:
                raise LLMError("HTTP 4xx")
            choice = (d.get("choices") or [{}])[0]
            text = ((choice.get("message") or {}).get("content") or "").strip()
            if text:
                break
        if not text:
            raise LLMError(f"empty reply (finish_reason={choice.get('finish_reason')})")
        ptok = (d.get("usage") or {}).get("prompt_tokens")
        sent = len(user) + len(system)
        if rung.check_truncation and isinstance(ptok, int) and sent >= TRUNCATION_MIN_CHARS \
                and (ptok * TRUNCATION_CHARS_PER_TOKEN < sent or ptok == TRUNCATION_CAP_TOKENS):
            raise LLMError(f"prompt truncated by the server ({ptok} tokens for {sent} chars)")
        return text

    def _post(self, rung: Rung, body: dict):
        req = urllib.request.Request(rung.base + "/chat/completions", data=json.dumps(body).encode(),
                                     headers={"Content-Type": "application/json"})
        if rung.key:
            req.add_unredirected_header("Authorization", f"Bearer {rung.key}")
        # No call outlives the scrape's deadline: a SIPB call that hung for its full 240 s after a slow start
        # finished a scrape at 322 s, after Claude Code had dropped the MCP call at 300 s (2026-10-18).
        left = getattr(self._tl, "t_end", float("inf")) - time.monotonic()
        if left <= 0:
            raise LLMError("deadline")
        try:
            with _open(req, max(1.0, min(self.call_timeout, left))) as r:
                d = json.loads(r.read())
        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
            if e.code in (400, 422) and "response_format" in body:
                return None
            raise LLMError(f"HTTP {e.code}") from e
        except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001
            raise LLMError(f"{type(e).__name__}: {e}") from e
        if not isinstance(d, dict) or not d.get("choices"):
            raise LLMError("bad response body")
        return d

    # one want on one rung, whole page or chunked
    def answer(self, rung: Rung, want: dict, md: str):
        if len(md) <= rung.one_shot:
            return self._one(rung, want, md), 1
        chunks = split_chunks(md, rung.chunk)
        return self._map_reduce(rung, want, chunks), len(chunks)

    def _one(self, rung, want, md):
        q = want["prompt"]
        if want["kind"] == "json":
            schema = want["schema"]
            sys_ = "Extract data from the page as JSON. Output only the JSON." + (
                f"\nSchema: {json.dumps(schema)}" if schema else "")
            return parse_json_text(self.chat(rung, sys_, f"{q}\n\nPage content:\n{md}".strip(), schema, True))
        quote = want["mode"] == "directQuote"
        out = self.chat(rung, LLM_QUOTE_SYS if quote else LLM_SYS, f"Page content:\n{md}\n\nQuestion: {q}")
        return LLM_ABSTAIN if quote and out.strip().strip('."\'') == LLM_NONE else out

    def _map_reduce(self, rung, want, chunks):
        q = want["prompt"]
        if want["kind"] == "json":
            schema = want["schema"]
            sys_ = ("Extract data from this EXCERPT of a longer page as JSON. Use null or an empty list for "
                    "anything the excerpt does not mention. Output only the JSON."
                    + (f"\nSchema: {json.dumps(schema)}" if schema else ""))
            parts = [parse_json_text(self.chat(rung, sys_, f"{q}\n\nExcerpt {i}/{len(chunks)}:\n{c}".strip(), schema, True))
                     for i, c in enumerate(chunks, 1)]
            red = ("Merge these partial JSON objects, extracted from consecutive excerpts of ONE page, into a single JSON "
                   "object. Prefer non-null values, join lists without duplicates. Output only the JSON."
                   + (f"\nSchema: {json.dumps(schema)}" if schema else ""))
            return parse_json_text(self.chat(rung, red, json.dumps(parts), schema, True))
        quote = want["mode"] == "directQuote"
        map_sys = ((LLM_QUOTE_SYS if quote else LLM_SYS)
                   + f" This is one excerpt of a longer page; reply exactly {LLM_NONE} if it holds nothing relevant.")
        hits = []
        for i, c in enumerate(chunks, 1):
            a = self.chat(rung, map_sys, f"Excerpt {i}/{len(chunks)}:\n{c}\n\nQuestion: {q}")
            if a.strip().strip('."\'') != LLM_NONE:
                hits.append(a)
        if not hits:
            return LLM_ABSTAIN
        if len(hits) == 1:
            return hits[0]
        joined = "\n".join(f"[{i}] {h}" for i, h in enumerate(hits, 1))
        return self.chat(rung, LLM_QUOTE_SYS if quote else LLM_SYS,
                         f"Candidate answers from different excerpts of one page:\n{joined}\n\n"
                         f"Question: {q}\n{'Pick the best candidate and output it verbatim.' if quote else 'Write the single final answer.'}")

    def run(self, wants: list[dict], md: str) -> tuple[dict, str, str]:
        """(fields to merge into data, name of the rung(s) that answered, warning or '')."""
        fields, used, errors = {}, [], []
        t_end = time.monotonic() + self.deadline
        self._tl.t_end = t_end
        for want in wants:
            key = "json" if want["kind"] == "json" else "answer"
            for rung in self.rungs:
                if time.monotonic() > t_end:
                    errors.append("deadline")
                    break
                try:
                    value, n = self.answer(rung, want, md)
                except LLMError as e:
                    errors.append(f"{rung.name}: {e}")
                    print(f"  llm rung {rung.name} failed: {e}", file=self.log, flush=True)
                    continue
                if want["kind"] == "query" and want["mode"] == "directQuote" and value != LLM_ABSTAIN \
                        and norm_text(value).strip("\"'“” ") not in norm_text(md):
                    errors.append(f"{rung.name}: quote not found in the page")
                    continue
                fields[key] = value
                used.append(f"{rung.name}{'x' + str(n) if n > 1 else ''}")
                break
        warning = ""
        if len(fields) < len(wants):
            warning = "LLM extraction failed (" + "; ".join(errors)[:300] + "); returning the page markdown instead."
        return fields, "+".join(used), warning


def build_extractor(env) -> Extractor | None:
    if (env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_LLM") or "").lower() == "off":
        return None
    sipb_base = _check_base("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_SIPB_BASE",
                            (env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_SIPB_BASE") or "http://127.0.0.1:8890/api").rstrip("/"))
    rungs = [Rung("sipb", sipb_base,
                  env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_SIPB_KEY", ""),
                  env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_SIPB_MODEL") or "qwen3.6:35b-a3b-q4_K_M",
                  SIPB_ONE_SHOT_CHARS, SIPB_CHUNK_CHARS, check_truncation=True)]
    lite_base = _check_base("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_LITELLM_BASE",
                            (env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_LITELLM_BASE") or "http://127.0.0.1:4000/v1").rstrip("/"))
    for m in (env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_LITELLM_MODELS") or "gemini-free,gemini-free-lite").split(","):
        if m.strip():
            rungs.append(Rung(m.strip(), lite_base, env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_LITELLM_KEY", ""), m.strip(),
                              BIG_ONE_SHOT_CHARS, BIG_CHUNK_CHARS))
    return Extractor(rungs, float(env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_LLM_DEADLINE") or 240))


class Router:
    def __init__(self, primary: Backend, fallback: Backend | None, timeout: float,
                 token: str = "", log=sys.stderr, extractor: Extractor | None = None,
                 search_timeout: float = 35.0, dev: DevSearch | None = None):
        self.extractor = extractor
        if extractor:
            extractor.log = log
        self.primary = primary
        self.fallback = fallback
        self.timeout = timeout
        self.search_timeout = search_timeout
        self.dev = dev
        self.token = token
        self.public_base = ""
        self.jobs: dict[str, str] = {}
        self.lock = threading.Lock()
        self.log = log

    def backend(self, name: str) -> Backend:
        return self.fallback if (name == "fallback" and self.fallback) else self.primary

    def remember(self, job_id: str, name: str) -> None:
        with self.lock:
            if len(self.jobs) >= MAX_JOBS:
                self.jobs.pop(next(iter(self.jobs)))
            self.jobs[job_id] = name

    def owner(self, path: str) -> str | None:
        m = UUID_RE.search(path)
        if not m:
            return None
        with self.lock:
            return self.jobs.get(m.group(0), "primary")

    def rewrite(self, reply: Reply, name: str) -> Reply:
        """Record job ids and point absolute API links back at the router."""
        doc = reply.json()
        if not isinstance(doc, dict):
            return reply
        changed = False
        if isinstance(doc.get("id"), str) and UUID_RE.fullmatch(doc["id"]):
            self.remember(doc["id"], name)

        def fix(holder: dict, key: str) -> None:
            nonlocal changed
            v = holder.get(key)
            if isinstance(v, str) and self.public_base:
                m = ABS_API_LINK_RE.match(v)
                if m:
                    j = UUID_RE.search(m.group(1))
                    if j:
                        self.remember(j.group(0), name)
                    holder[key] = self.public_base + m.group(1)
                    changed = True

        fix(doc, "url")
        fix(doc, "next")
        if isinstance(doc.get("data"), dict):
            fix(doc["data"], "next")
        if changed:
            reply.body = json.dumps(doc).encode()
        return reply

    def handle(self, method: str, path: str, headers: dict, body: bytes | None) -> tuple[Reply, str]:
        if self.dev and self.fallback is None:  # with a commercial fallback its own index answers, as before
            kind = dev_route(method, path, body)
            if kind:
                return self._developer(kind, method, path, body)
        if self.extractor and method == "POST" and path.split("?", 1)[0].rstrip("/").endswith("/scrape"):
            try:
                doc = json.loads(body or b"{}")
            except ValueError:
                doc = None
            split = wanted_formats(doc) if isinstance(doc, dict) else None
            if split:
                return self._scrape_with_llm(method, path, headers, doc, *split)
        return self._forward(method, path, headers, body)

    def _developer(self, kind: str, method: str, path: str, body: bytes | None) -> tuple[Reply, str]:
        t0 = time.monotonic()
        if kind == "direct":
            params, why = parse_dev_request(method, path, body)
        else:  # POST /v2/search with categories ["developer"]: `limit` is the result count
            doc = json.loads(body)
            limit = _dev_int(doc.get("limit"), 5)
            params, why = None, "limit must be an integer 1-100"
            if limit is not None and 1 <= limit <= 100:
                params, why = parse_dev_request("POST", path, json.dumps({"query": doc.get("query"), "k": limit}).encode())
        if params is None:
            status, out, note = 400, {"success": False, "error": f"firecrawl-router: {why}"}, why
        else:
            status, out, note = self.dev.search(params)
            if kind == "category" and status == 200:
                ignored = [k for k in ("scrapeOptions", "sources", "tbs", "location", "country")
                           if doc.get(k) not in (None, "", [], {})]
                warnings = ([out["warning"]] if "warning" in out else []) + (
                    [f"ignored for the developer category: {', '.join(ignored)}"] if ignored else [])
                out = {"success": True, "source": "github", "data": {"web": dev_web_results(out)}, "creditsUsed": 0,
                       **({"warning": "; ".join(warnings)} if warnings else {})}
        reply = Reply(status, {"Content-Type": "application/json"}, json.dumps(out).encode())
        if status == 429 and "retryAfter" in out:
            reply.headers["Retry-After"] = str(out["retryAfter"])
        self._log(method, path, "github", reply, t0, note)
        return reply, "github"

    def _scrape_with_llm(self, method, path, headers, doc, kept, wants) -> tuple[Reply, str]:
        t0 = time.monotonic()
        has_md = any((f.get("type") if isinstance(f, dict) else f) == "markdown" for f in kept)
        up = {k: v for k, v in doc.items() if k not in ("jsonOptions", "queryOptions")}
        up["formats"] = kept if has_md else kept + ["markdown"]
        reply, backend = self._forward(method, path, headers, json.dumps(up).encode())
        out = reply.json()
        data = out.get("data") if isinstance(out, dict) else None
        md = data.get("markdown") if isinstance(data, dict) else None
        if reply.status == 200 and isinstance(data, dict) and isinstance(md, str) and not md.strip():
            data["warning"] = (data.get("warning", "") + " The page has no content, so there is nothing to extract from.").strip()
            reply.body = json.dumps(out).encode()
            reply.headers = {k: v for k, v in reply.headers.items() if k.lower() != "content-length"}
            reply.headers["X-Firecrawl-LLM"] = "none"
            return reply, backend
        if reply.status != 200 or not isinstance(md, str) or not md.strip():
            return reply, backend
        fields, used, warning = self.extractor.run(wants, md)
        data.update(fields)
        if warning:
            data["warning"] = (data.get("warning", "") + " " + warning).strip()
        elif not has_md:
            data.pop("markdown", None)
        reply.body = json.dumps(out).encode()
        reply.headers = {k: v for k, v in reply.headers.items() if k.lower() != "content-length"}
        reply.headers["X-Firecrawl-LLM"] = used or "none"
        self._log(method, path, backend, reply, t0, f"llm: {used or 'FAILED'}; {len(md)} chars")
        return reply, backend

    def _forward(self, method: str, path: str, headers: dict, body: bytes | None) -> tuple[Reply, str]:
        t0 = time.monotonic()
        # Cap /search: a hung SearXNG used to sit on FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_TIMEOUT (120 s) and
        # trip Cursor MCP -32001 before the ladder could move on (commercial off, 2026-10-22).
        cap = self.search_timeout if search_path(path) else None
        timeout = request_timeout(body, self.timeout, cap=cap)
        owner = self.owner(path)
        if owner is not None:
            b = self.backend(owner)
            reply = self.rewrite(call(b, method, path, headers, body, timeout), b.name)
            self._log(method, path, b.name, reply, t0, "job owner")
            return reply, b.name
        first = call(self.primary, method, path, headers, body, timeout)
        reason = fallback_reason(path, first)
        if not reason or not self.fallback:
            self._log(method, path, "primary", first, t0, reason and f"{reason}; no fallback")
            return self.rewrite(first, "primary"), "primary"
        second = call(self.fallback, method, path, headers, body, timeout)
        if 200 <= second.status < 300 or first.status == 0:
            self._log(method, path, "fallback", second, t0, reason)
            return self.rewrite(second, "fallback"), "fallback"
        self._log(method, path, "primary", first, t0, f"{reason}; fallback HTTP {second.status or second.error}")
        return self.rewrite(first, "primary"), "primary"

    def _log(self, method, path, backend, reply, t0, note) -> None:
        status = reply.status or "ERR"
        line = f"{time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')} {method} {path.split('?', 1)[0]} -> {backend} {status} {time.monotonic() - t0:.1f}s"
        if note:
            line += f" [{note}]"
        print(line, file=self.log, flush=True)


def make_handler(router: Router):
    class Handler(http.server.BaseHTTPRequestHandler):
        protocol_version = "HTTP/1.1"

        def log_message(self, *_):
            pass

        def _serve(self):
            if router.token:
                auth = self.headers.get("Authorization") or ""
                if not hmac.compare_digest(auth, f"Bearer {router.token}"):
                    self._send(401, {"Content-Type": "application/json"}, b'{"success":false,"error":"unauthorized"}')
                    return
            else:
                # No token: a browser page could otherwise reach the router through the
                # operator's own resolver (DNS rebinding). Accept only a Host that names
                # this loopback server: loopback hostname and the bound port (2026-10-22).
                host = (self.headers.get("Host") or "").strip()
                name, sep, port = host.rpartition(":")
                name = name.strip("[]") if sep else host
                bound = str(self.server.server_address[1])
                if name not in LOOPBACK_URL_HOSTS or port not in ((bound, "80") if bound == "80" else (bound,)):
                    self._send(403, {"Content-Type": "application/json"},
                               b'{"success":false,"error":"firecrawl-router: host not allowed"}')
                    return
            n = int(self.headers.get("Content-Length") or 0)
            body = self.rfile.read(n) if n else None
            if not self.path.startswith("/"):  # ".evil.example/x" appended to a base URL names another host
                self._send(400, {"Content-Type": "application/json"},
                           b'{"success":false,"error":"firecrawl-router: request target must start with /"}')
                return
            reply, backend = router.handle(self.command, self.path, dict(self.headers), body)
            if reply.status == 0:
                self._send(502, {"Content-Type": "application/json"},
                           json.dumps({"success": False, "error": f"firecrawl-router: {reply.error}"}).encode())
                return
            hdrs = {k: v for k, v in reply.headers.items()
                    if k.lower() not in HOP_HEADERS and k.lower() != "content-encoding"}
            hdrs["X-Firecrawl-Backend"] = backend
            self._send(reply.status, hdrs, reply.body)

        def _send(self, status, headers, body):
            self.send_response(status)
            for k, v in headers.items():
                self.send_header(k, v)
            self.send_header("Content-Length", str(len(body)))
            self.end_headers()
            self.wfile.write(body)

        do_GET = do_POST = do_DELETE = do_PUT = do_PATCH = _serve

    return Handler


def build_router(env, token: str) -> Router:
    primary_url = (env.get("FIRECRAWL_SELFHOST_URL") or "").rstrip("/")
    if not primary_url:
        sys.exit("firecrawl-router: FIRECRAWL_SELFHOST_URL is not set")
    primary = Backend("primary", _check_base("FIRECRAWL_SELFHOST_URL", primary_url),
                      env.get("FIRECRAWL_SELFHOST_API_KEY", ""))
    fallback = None
    fb_key = env.get("FIRECRAWL_API_KEY", "")
    if fb_key and env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_FALLBACK", "").lower() != "off":
        fb_url = (env.get("FIRECRAWL_FALLBACK_URL") or "https://api.firecrawl.dev").rstrip("/")
        fallback = Backend("fallback", _check_base("FIRECRAWL_FALLBACK_URL", fb_url), fb_key)
    search_timeout = float(env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_SEARCH_TIMEOUT") or 35)
    dev = None
    if env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_DEVELOPER", "").lower() != "off":
        gh_base = (env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_GITHUB_BASE") or "https://api.github.com").rstrip("/")
        secret = env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_GITHUB_SECRET") or "GITHUB_TOKEN"
        if not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*", secret):
            sys.exit("firecrawl-router: FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_GITHUB_SECRET must be an upper-case sudo-secretspec name")
        dev = DevSearch(_check_base("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_GITHUB_BASE", gh_base), secret=secret,
                        token=env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_GITHUB_KEY", ""), timeout=min(15.0, search_timeout),
                        budget=search_timeout)
    return Router(primary, fallback, float(env.get("FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_TIMEOUT") or 120), token,
                  extractor=build_extractor(env), search_timeout=search_timeout, dev=dev)


def serve(router: Router, listen: str, require_loopback: bool = False) -> http.server.ThreadingHTTPServer:
    """Bind and start serving. With require_loopback, the address actually bound must be loopback: the
    check runs after bind and before the first request can be accepted (2026-10-20), so a resolver that
    maps "localhost" elsewhere gets no window at all; the socket is closed and SystemExit(2) raised."""
    host, _, port = listen.rpartition(":")
    srv = http.server.ThreadingHTTPServer((host or "127.0.0.1", int(port or 0)), make_handler(router))
    srv.daemon_threads = True
    if require_loopback and not ipaddress.ip_address(srv.server_address[0]).is_loopback:
        bound = srv.server_address[0]
        srv.server_close()
        print(f"firecrawl-router: refusing to serve without a token on {bound}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        raise SystemExit(2)
    router.public_base = f"http://{srv.server_address[0]}:{srv.server_address[1]}"
    threading.Thread(target=srv.serve_forever, daemon=True).start()
    return srv


# serve() binds AF_INET, so IPv6 spellings can never bind here; they are refused (fail closed).
LOOPBACK_HOSTS = ("127.0.0.1", "localhost")


def is_loopback_listen(listen: str) -> bool:
    return listen.rpartition(":")[0] in LOOPBACK_HOSTS


def main(argv=None) -> int:
    argv = list(sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv)
    child = []
    if "--" in argv:
        i = argv.index("--")
        argv, child = argv[:i], argv[i + 1:]
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="firecrawl-router", description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
    ap.add_argument("--listen", default="127.0.0.1:0", help="HOST:PORT (default 127.0.0.1:0, ephemeral)")
    ap.add_argument("--open", action="store_true", help="no bearer token (loopback --listen only)")
    args = ap.parse_args(argv)
    if (args.open or not child) and not is_loopback_listen(args.listen):
        ap.error("a run without a bearer token (--open, or no child command) needs a loopback --listen address")

    token = secrets.token_urlsafe(32) if child and not args.open else ""
    router = build_router(os.environ, token)
    # defence in depth: the string check above passed; the address actually bound is checked before
    # the server accepts anything (a resolver could map "localhost" elsewhere)
    srv = serve(router, args.listen, require_loopback=not token)
    fb = _origin(router.fallback.base) if router.fallback else "none"
    print(f"firecrawl-router: {router.public_base} primary={_origin(router.primary.base)} fallback={fb}",
          file=sys.stderr, flush=True)

    if not child:
        try:
            threading.Event().wait()
        except KeyboardInterrupt:
            return 0
    hidden = ("FIRECRAWL_SELFHOST_API_KEY", "FIRECRAWL_SELFHOST_URL", "FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_SIPB_KEY", "FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_LITELLM_KEY",
              "FIRECRAWL_ROUTER_GITHUB_KEY")
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k not in hidden}
    env["FIRECRAWL_API_URL"] = router.public_base
    env["FIRECRAWL_API_KEY"] = token or "router-open"
    proc = subprocess.Popen(child, env=env)
    for sig in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGHUP):
        signal.signal(sig, lambda s, _f: proc.send_signal(s))
    rc = proc.wait()
    srv.shutdown()
    return rc if rc >= 0 else 128 - rc


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
